@page "/privacy-policy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Read this privacy policy to learn how data is collected, processed, protected, and managed." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="page-container page-section article-shell privacy-page">
    <BackToHome />

    <header class="privacy-intro">
        <div class="privacy-title-row">
            <span class="privacy-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <AppIcon Name="lock" />
            </span>
            <div>
                <h1 class="text-page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="privacy-updated text-caption">Last updated: February 2026</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="privacy-intro-note text-caption">
            How this archive handles data, analytics, cookies, and privacy-related requests.
        </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="privacy-contents" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
        <span class="privacy-contents-label text-caption">On this page</span>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#scope" data-enhance-nav="false">Scope</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#information" data-enhance-nav="false">Information</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#use" data-enhance-nav="false">Use</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#analytics" data-enhance-nav="false">Analytics</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#retention" data-enhance-nav="false">Retention</a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy#rights" data-enhance-nav="false">Rights</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="privacy-document">
        <section id="scope" class="privacy-section">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><span>Scope and Purpose</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                This Privacy Policy explains how personal data is collected, used, stored,
                and protected when using this website and related services.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body">
                By accessing or using this website, users acknowledge the practices described
                in this policy.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="information" class="privacy-section">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><span>Information That May Be Collected</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                Depending on usage, the following categories of information may be collected:
                technical data (for example IP address, browser type, device type, and pages visited),
                usage analytics, and information voluntarily submitted through contact forms or email.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body">
                Sensitive personal data is not intentionally requested unless explicitly required for
                a specific service.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="use" class="privacy-section">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><span>How Information Is Used</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                Collected information may be used to operate and improve the website, maintain service
                performance and security, understand usage trends, respond to inquiries, and comply with
                legal obligations.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body">
                Information is processed only for legitimate purposes and is not sold to third parties.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="analytics" class="privacy-section">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><span>Analytics, Cookies, and Third-Party Services</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                This website may use cookies or similar technologies for functionality, security,
                and analytics. Analytics providers or infrastructure partners may process limited
                technical data according to their own privacy terms.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body">
                Users can manage or disable cookies through browser settings. Disabling cookies may
                affect certain website features.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention" class="privacy-section">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span><span>Data Retention and Security</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                Data is retained only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes described in
                this policy or to meet legal requirements.
            </p>
            <p class="text-body">
                Reasonable technical and organizational safeguards are applied to protect data.
                However, no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be fully secure.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="rights" class="privacy-section privacy-section-contact">
            <h2 class="text-section-title"><span class="privacy-section-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span><span>User Rights and Contact</span></h2>
            <p class="text-body">
                Subject to applicable laws, users may have rights to access, correct, delete,
                or restrict processing of their personal data. To submit a privacy-related request,
                use the contact channel below.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-contact text-body"><strong>Contact Email:</strong> <a class="link-muted" href="mailto:contact@sametcc.me">contact@sametcc.me</a></p>
            <p class="privacy-update-note text-caption text-muted">
                This policy may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the website after
                changes are published constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
            </p>
        </section>
    </article>
</div>
